    "## 4. Foundation model and one-shot classifier\n",
    "\n",
    "The model has two parts:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Frozen foundation-model backbone** (`FoundationModel`): CLIP, SigLIP, or DINOv2 turns an image (or a text prompt) into an L2-normalized embedding. It is never trained, so the 16 labeled images can't overfit it.\n",
    "- **Trainable prototype head** (`PrototypeHead`): one weight vector per class, compared with image embeddings by cosine similarity. It starts from the zero-shot text prototypes fused with the support-image prototypes and is trained on augmented support views, with an L2 term that keeps it near its starting point.\n",
    "\n",
    "The cell below writes `oneshot_lib.py` next to the notebook so that `inference.py` in your GitHub repo imports exactly the same code. If you edit it, restart the kernel or run `importlib.reload(oneshot_lib)`. It also contains the **test-time** pieces: test-time augmentation and transductive refinement (soft k-means on unlabeled test features, with class-balanced Sinkhorn assignments, anchored to the prototypes)."
   ]
